@aEgoist The Agnes phrasing is in. The branch is rebased onto current upstream/main and carries your words as a learned cap, same as 100milionseek's and Coarena's: [fix/5696-image-count-fallback](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5696-image-count-fallback) at `206c9bdb3`.

- `TestImageCapLearnedFromAgnesWords` (new) learns the cap from both your exact body and a plain `{"error":{"message":…}}` shape; with the phrasing set aside by hand it fails (`no cap learned from …`), with it it passes, beside `TestImageCountGroupFallback` and `TestImageCountRefusalControls` still passing. `go vet` clean; the package suite is green except `TestClaudeClientCacheAbsentUnchanged`, which fails the same way on a tree without these changes on this machine (the known `/bin/sh`-is-bash environment, #3280).

So an `agnes-cn` member over its cap now falls through to the next candidate with the request intact, and `magpie provider set agnes-cn max-images=4` stays as the direct-request workaround. Waiting for the maintainer to pick it up, as ever — nothing more needed from your side. The plugin-side preset you asked for in magpie-plugin-agnes#1 would still be the better fix for that provider alone; the gateway learning covers every vendor whose words land in this class.
